                <pb facs="0271" n="183" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg183"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Conger.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-11-23"><hi rendition="#italic">November 23,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hay states that the views of this Government on the payment of the Chinese
                    indemnity in silver were stated in Department’s telegram of July 11, 1902
                    (printed below). In accepting the decision reached by the Chinese Government the
                    United States Government expects the same treatment as the other interested
                    powers.</p>



                <xi:include href="d159-a1.xml" xpointer="d159-a1"/>
            </div>
